              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "To log in to your **My Service Canada Account (MSCA)**, you can access the official Government of Canada portal directly:\n\n\ud83d\udc49 **[Go to the My Service Canada Account (MSCA) Login Page](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-service-canada-account.html)**\n\n---\n\n### How to Sign In\nOnce on the login page, you can choose one of three secure ways to access your account:\n\n1. **Sign-In Partner (Recommended & Easiest):**\n   * Log in using your existing online banking credentials (e.g., RBC, TD, Scotiabank, BMO, CIBC, Tangerine, etc.) via Interac. \n   * *No financial details are shared with the government; this is strictly used to securely verify your identity.*\n\n2. **GCKey:**\n   * Log in using a government-issued GCKey username and password. If you don't have one, you can register for one on the spot.\n\n3. **Provincial Digital ID (Select Provinces Only):**\n   * If you reside in **Alberta** or **British Columbia**, you can use your **Alberta.ca Account** or your **BC Services Card** to log in.\n\n---\n\n### What You Can Do Once Logged In\nOnce you sign in, you can manage and view details for several federal services:\n* **Employment Insurance (EI):** Check your claim status, submit reports, and view past claims.\n* **Canada Pension Plan (CPP) & Old Age Security (OAS):** View estimated retirement benefits and manage monthly payments.\n* **Canadian Dental Care Plan (CDCP):** Apply for or renew your dental benefits.\n* **Social Insurance Number (SIN):** View your digital SIN confirmation securely.\n* **Direct Deposit:** Set up or update your banking info to get your federal payments directly into your bank account.\n\n### First Time Registering?\nIf you are logging in for the very first time, you will need to register and verify your identity. You will typically need:\n* Your **Social Insurance Number (SIN)**.\n* Your date of birth.\n* A **Personal Access Code (PAC)** (which you may have received in the mail, or can request online or by calling Service Canada).",
